   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Spark Streaming With Kafka (Dashboard)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In this notebook we implement a real-time streaming pipeline that ingests weather and air-quality events from Apache Kafka, processes them with Spark Structured Streaming, and writes the results to PostgreSQL so they can be visualised live in Apache Superset.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The pipeline uses a micro-batch architecture that fits well with the roughly one-minute ingestion rate of the data sources:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Kafka  →  Spark Structured Streaming  →  foreachBatch  →  PostgreSQL  →  Superset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Two Kafka topics are consumed:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`weather-barcelona`** — current weather observations (temperature, wind speed, weather code, …)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`airquality-barcelona`** — air-quality monitoring station metadata and sensor readings\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Purpose\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Run Spark Structured Streaming against Kafka weather and air-quality topics and publish dashboard-ready live evidence.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Inputs\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Kafka topics `weather-barcelona` and `airquality-barcelona`, with Spark runtime and optional dashboard sink configuration.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Validation / quality checks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The notebook validates Kafka/Spark connectivity, parsed schemas, streaming query status, and dashboard sink readiness.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Transformation / cleaning logic\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Kafka values are parsed by topic-specific schemas, split into weather and air-quality streams, and the dashboard stream is written to the configured sink.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Metadata and lineage fields\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Launch evidence tracks source assets, check message/status, created time, schema version, and dashboard dependency status.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Output assets\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Streaming console evidence, dashboard sink rows, and `exploitation_analytics.streaming_dashboard_launch_log` from the companion Airflow validation DAG.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## RBAC / service user used\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The notebook uses Kafka reader, Spark, PostgreSQL/dashboard, and ClickHouse consumption credentials configured through environment variables.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Notebook-DAG alignment note\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The notebook owns the live streaming dashboard logic, while `consumption_zone_streaming_dashboard_trigger` validates dependencies and records launch evidence. They are aligned as companion consumption evidence and the notebook does not import DAG functions.\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Execution Notes and Batch Logging\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This notebook is intentionally long-running because Spark Structured Streaming calls `foreachBatch` once per micro-batch. The batch logs print each micro-batch id, raw row count, cleaned row count, rejected row count, and PostgreSQL sink confirmation so dashboard writes can be audited from notebook output.\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Importing Useful Libraries**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Airflow Consumption DAG Alignment**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The notebook is the interactive, long-running Spark Structured Streaming runtime. The Airflow DAG `consumption_zone_streaming_dashboard_trigger` intentionally does not run the infinite streaming loop inside a worker; it validates the Kafka topics, Spark master, and notebook mount, then records a quick launch/health event in `exploitation_analytics.streaming_dashboard_launch_log` with `source_system`, `source_assets`, `created_at`, `schema_version`, `consumption_task`, `dashboard_name`, and `trigger_status`.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Standard libraries plus the Kafka-Python consumer for ad-hoc inspection, `boto3` for optional MinIO access, and `python-dotenv` to load credentials from a `.env` file.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 1,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {\n",
    "    \"ExecuteTime\": {\n",
    "     \"end_time\": \"2026-03-18T16:57:02.361590900Z\",\n",
    "     \"start_time\": \"2026-03-18T16:57:02.039234200Z\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    \"scrolled\": true\n",
    "   },\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from kafka import KafkaConsumer\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from dotenv import load_dotenv\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql.functions import col, from_json, explode\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql.types import *\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import json\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import boto3\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import io\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import time\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Load .env file\\n\",\n",
    "    \"load_dotenv()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Read environment variables\\n\",\n",
    "    \"endpoint = os.getenv(\\\"MINIO_ENDPOINT\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"MINIO_ROLE = \\\"reader\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if MINIO_ROLE == \\\"admin\\\":\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    access_key = os.getenv(\\\"MINIO_ACCESS_KEY\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    secret_key = os.getenv(\\\"MINIO_SECRET_KEY\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    role_prefix = MINIO_ROLE.upper()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    access_key = os.getenv(f\\\"MINIO_{role_prefix}_ACCESS_KEY\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    secret_key = os.getenv(f\\\"MINIO_{role_prefix}_SECRET_KEY\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if not endpoint or not access_key or not secret_key:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Missing MinIO {MINIO_ROLE} credentials in environment\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Deserializer function\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def deserialize(m):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return json.loads(m.decode(\\\"utf-8\\\"))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 2,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"data\": {\n",
    "      \"text/plain\": [\n",
    "       \"['source_system',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'source_assets',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'created_at',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'schema_version',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'consumption_task',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'dashboard_name',\\n\",\n",
    "       \" 'trigger_status']\"\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "     },\n",
    "     \"execution_count\": 2,\n",
    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"execute_result\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Airflow DAG metadata contract for the quick dashboard launch/health event.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# The interactive notebook keeps running the actual Spark streaming query below.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DASHBOARD_LAUNCH_LOG_COLUMNS = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"source_system\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"source_assets\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"created_at\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"schema_version\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"consumption_task\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"dashboard_name\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"trigger_status\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DASHBOARD_LAUNCH_LOG_COLUMNS\\n\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Creating the Spark Session**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"We connect to the existing Spark cluster and declare the required JARs:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `spark-sql-kafka-0-10` — Structured Streaming connector for Kafka.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- `postgresql` — JDBC driver used later to write micro-batches to PostgreSQL.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> **Note:** The first cell downloads the Kafka connector JAR from Maven Central.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"> This takes several minutes on the first run; subsequent runs use the cached JAR.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 3,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"spark = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    SparkSession.builder\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .appName(\\\"BDM_Streaming\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .master(\\\"spark://spark-master:7077\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .config(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"spark.jars.packages\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\",\\\".join([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Downloads the Kafka connector on first run; cached in ~/.ivy2 afterward\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"org.apache.spark:spark-sql-kafka-0-10_2.13:4.1.1\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # Postgre JDBC driver\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            \\\"org.postgresql:postgresql:42.7.3\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .getOrCreate()\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Reading the Raw Kafka Stream**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"We subscribe to both topics simultaneously using a single `readStream` source. Kafka delivers all messages as raw bytes. The `value` column will be parsed against explicit schemas in the next steps.`startingOffsets: earliest` ensures we replay all historical messages on restart, which is safe because the JDBC sink uses `append` mode and the checkpoint prevents re-processing.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 4,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"raw_stream = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    spark.readStream\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .format(\\\"kafka\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"kafka.bootstrap.servers\\\", \\\"kafka:9092\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"subscribe\\\", \\\"weather-barcelona, airquality-barcelona\\\") # Kafka Consumers\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"startingOffsets\\\", \\\"earliest\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .load()\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Splitting Streams by Topic**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Kafka attaches a `topic` column to every row. We filter on it to produce two independent streaming DataFrames that can be processed with different schemas.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 5,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"weather_stream = raw_stream.filter(col(\\\"topic\\\") == \\\"weather-barcelona\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"air_stream     = raw_stream.filter(col(\\\"topic\\\") == \\\"airquality-barcelona\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Defining and Applying Schemas**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Weather stream** — flat JSON object with seven fields. We parse the `value` bytes, apply the schema, and flatten the result into a regular DataFrame (`weather_events`).\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 6,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Weather Schema\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weather_schema = StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"interval\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"is_day\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"temperature\\\", DoubleType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"time\\\", TimestampType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"weathercode\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"winddirection\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"windspeed\\\", DoubleType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Weather Events\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weather_events = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    weather_stream\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .select(from_json(col(\\\"value\\\").cast(\\\"string\\\"), weather_schema).alias(\\\"data\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .select(\\\"data.*\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Air-quality stream** — JSON array of station objects with nested sub-documents (`country`, `owner`, `provider`, `coordinates`, `datetimeFirst`, `datetimeLast`). We:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Parse the array with `from_json`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. `explode` it so each station becomes its own row.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Select only the columns relevant to a dashboard (station identity, location, timestamps, and sensors), discarding `licenses`, `bounds`, and `instruments`.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 7,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Air Schema\\n\",\n",
    "    \"air_schema = ArrayType(StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"id\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"name\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"locality\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"timezone\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"country\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"id\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"code\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"name\\\", StringType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ])),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"owner\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"id\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"name\\\", StringType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ])),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"provider\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"id\\\", IntegerType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"name\\\", StringType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ])),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"isMobile\\\", BooleanType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"isMonitor\\\", BooleanType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"coordinates\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"latitude\\\", DoubleType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"longitude\\\", DoubleType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ])),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"instruments\\\", ArrayType(StringType())),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"sensors\\\", ArrayType(StringType())),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"licenses\\\", ArrayType(StringType())),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"bounds\\\", ArrayType(DoubleType())),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"datetimeFirst\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"utc\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"local\\\", StringType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ])),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    StructField(\\\"datetimeLast\\\", StructType([\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"utc\\\", StringType()),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        StructField(\\\"local\\\", StringType())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ]))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"]))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Apply Air Schema\\n\",\n",
    "    \"parsed = air_stream.select(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    from_json(col(\\\"value\\\").cast(\\\"string\\\"), air_schema).alias(\\\"data\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Explode rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"air_rows = parsed.select(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    explode(col(\\\"data\\\")).alias(\\\"station\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Air Events (We are not interested in all attributes)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"air_events = air_rows.select(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.id\\\").alias(\\\"station_id\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.name\\\").alias(\\\"station_name\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.locality\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.timezone\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.isMobile\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.isMonitor\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.coordinates.latitude\\\").alias(\\\"latitude\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.coordinates.longitude\\\").alias(\\\"longitude\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.country.name\\\").alias(\\\"country\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.provider.name\\\").alias(\\\"provider\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.owner.name\\\").alias(\\\"owner\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.datetimeFirst.local\\\").alias(\\\"datetimeFirst\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.datetimeLast.local\\\").alias(\\\"datetimeLast\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    col(\\\"station.sensors\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    #col(\\\"station.licenses\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    #col(\\\"station.bounds\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    #col(\\\"station.instruments\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Console Sink — Observing Live Events**\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Before writing to PostgreSQL it is useful to verify that the schemas are parsed correctly by printing micro-batches to the container's stdout. Because the output goes to the JupyterLab process log rather than the notebook, you need to run the following command in a terminal to see it:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```bash\\n\",\n",
    "    \"docker compose logs jupyter -f\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The queries are started below and must be explicitly stopped with `.stop()` before launching the PostgreSQL sink.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 8,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Write to console — stop query_weather.stop()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"query_weather = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    weather_events\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .writeStream\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .format(\\\"console\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"truncate\\\", False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"numRows\\\", 10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .start()\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 9,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Write to console — stop with query_air.stop()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"query_air = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    air_events\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .writeStream\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .format(\\\"console\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"truncate\\\", False)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"numRows\\\", 10)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .start()\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"Stop both console queries once the output looks correct.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 10,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"query_weather.stop()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"query_air.stop()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Real-time Dashboard Construction\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"In the end, we decided to use `weather-barcelona` only for the live dashboard because its flat schema maps directly to a relational table without any array expansion. The sink function `write_to_postgres` is called once per micro-batch by `foreachBatch`. It appends the batch DataFrame to the `weather_events` table in the `analytics` PostgreSQL database that Superset reads from. A checkpoint directory is required by Spark Structured Streaming to track committed Kafka offsets across restarts and reduce reprocessing risk; because the JDBC sink appends rows, this should not be described as exactly-once or duplicate-free.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 11,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def write_to_postgres(batch_df, batch_id):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    raw_count = batch_df.count()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"[micro-batch {batch_id}] received rows={raw_count}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # --- Preprocessing / Data validation ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cleaned_df = batch_df.filter(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        (col(\\\"temperature\\\").between(-50, 60)) &\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        (col(\\\"windspeed\\\").between(0, 150)) &\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        (col(\\\"winddirection\\\").between(0, 360)) &\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        (col(\\\"interval\\\") > 0) &\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        (col(\\\"time\\\").isNotNull())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    )\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cleaned_count = cleaned_df.count()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"[micro-batch {batch_id}] cleaned rows={cleaned_count}; rejected={raw_count - cleaned_count}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if cleaned_count == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"[micro-batch {batch_id}] skipped PostgreSQL write because the cleaned batch is empty\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # --- Write to PostgreSQL ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cleaned_df.write \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .format(\\\"jdbc\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .mode(\\\"append\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .option(\\\"url\\\", \\\"jdbc:postgresql://postgres-analytics:5432/analytics\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .option(\\\"driver\\\", \\\"org.postgresql.Driver\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .option(\\\"dbtable\\\", \\\"weather_events\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .option(\\\"user\\\", \\\"superset\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .option(\\\"password\\\", \\\"superset\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        .save()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"[micro-batch {batch_id}] wrote {cleaned_count} rows to PostgreSQL table weather_events\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Write a real-time table\\n\",\n",
    "    \"query = (\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    weather_events.writeStream\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .foreachBatch(write_to_postgres)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .option(\\\"checkpointLocation\\\", \\\"/tmp/checkpoints/weather\\\") # Save the temporal file in the jupyter container\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .outputMode(\\\"append\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .start()\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Monitoring the streaming query**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The cells below allow us to inspect whether the query is still running (`isActive`), print the schema to confirm the structure sent to PostgreSQL, and check the current query status (e.g. waiting for new Kafka messages vs. actively processing a batch).\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
